/**
 * @page cpptests C++ tests
 *
 * @brief Native unit tests for the host-runnable parts of @c libbotanik, built on
 *        [doctest](https://github.com/doctest/doctest).
 *
 * The framework ships as a single vendored header (`tests/vendor/doctest.h`), so
 * there is nothing to fetch or install. Tests compile and run only in the
 * @c SIMULATOR build - they link the host `botanik` library and execute natively.
 *
 * @section cpptests_run Building & running
 *
 * From a configured SIMULATOR build tree:
 *
 *     cmake -B build -DBOTANIK_TARGET=SIMULATOR   # once
 *     make -C build check                         # build the suite + run it
 *
 * `make check` builds the `botanik_tests` binary and runs it through CTest with
 * failures echoed inline. Equivalent lower-level invocations:
 *
 *     make -C build botanik_tests          # just build the binary
 *     ./build/tests/botanik_tests          # run directly (doctest CLI)
 *     ./build/tests/botanik_tests -s       # ...with every successful check shown
 *     ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
 *
 * The raw binary accepts the full doctest command line - e.g.
 * `-tc="format_float*"` to run matching cases, `-ltc` to list them.
 *
 * @section cpptests_suites Suites
 *
 * - @ref test_text.cpp - the fixed-point `format_float()` (the stand-in for the
 *   missing `%f`) and the "N u ago" `format_age()` duration formatter.
 * - @ref test_time.cpp - 32-bit uptime rollover projection and the
 *   calendar/UNIX conversion, checked for internal consistency against an
 *   independent date algorithm rather than a pinned wall-clock date.
 * - @ref test_parser.cpp - the input parser decoding raw byte streams into
 *   events (CSI, Alt, and function-key escape sequences).
 * - @ref test_line_buffer.cpp - the fixed-capacity circular line buffer behind
 *   the scrollback (soft-wrap splitting, newest-first access).
 * - @ref test_logger.cpp / @ref test_writer.cpp / @ref test_filters.cpp - the
 *   logger: dual token-bucket rate limiting, the writers, and the topic filters.
 * - @ref test_alarms.cpp - the alarm model (raise/clear, the platform/site bit
 *   splice, sorting).
 * - @ref test_serial.cpp - the `BufferedSerial` ring buffer.
 * - @ref test_shell.cpp - command dispatch and the built-in handlers.
 * - @ref test_sizes.cpp - living documentation of the in-memory footprint of the
 *   long-lived UI and PLC objects (see below).
 *
 * @section cpptests_sizes Object sizes
 *
 * The OPTA core is RAM-constrained, so `test_sizes.cpp` prints the size of the
 * "big" structures on every run and fails only if one grows past a generous
 * budget. The figures below are from the x86-64 host build; the ARM target
 * differs (notably 4-byte pointers/`size_t`), and the page sizes are dominated by
 * config-driven line/log buffers, so they track the `Config::*` buffer knobs
 * rather than code changes.
 *
 * | Structure                  | Host size (bytes) |
 * |----------------------------|------------------:|
 * | `Terminal::AnsiTerminal`   |               264 |
 * | `Terminal::TextEditor`     |               976 |
 * | `Terminal::InputParser`    |               112 |
 * | `Pages::HomePage<…>`       |            20'232 |
 * | `Pages::StatusPage<…>`     |             1'216 |
 * | `Pages::LogsPage`          |            50'504 |
 * | `Pages::ShellPage`         |            51'520 |
 * | `PlcIO::PlcInput<…>`       |                16 |
 * | `PlcIO::PlcOutput<…>`      |             8'648 |
 *
 * Run `./build/tests/botanik_tests -s` for the authoritative, current numbers.
 */
